  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Majeti Krishna Rao vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 30 July, 2020 Author: Cheekati Manavendranath Roy Bench: Cheekati Manavendranath Roy The Hon'Ble Sri Justice Cheekati Manavendranath Roy Crl.P.Nos.1432, 2359, 2366, 2368, 2369, 2943 & 2948 of 2020 Common Order:",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "When these matters are taken up for hearing, both the learned counsel for the petitioners in all these petitions and the learned Additional Public Prosecutor would submit that these matters are squarely covered by earlier decisions of this court, whereunder the accused against whom similar cases were registered on the basis of similar set of facts were [LEAKAGE_MASK] by this Court as the prosecution is not maintainable against them under law and also on the ground that Tobacco products would not fall within the definition of 'food' as defined under Section 3(i)(j) of FSS Act and that the police are not authorized to register the crime and investigate the same and to file the charge sheet.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "When these matters are taken up for hearing, both the learned counsel for the petitioners in all these petitions and the learned Additional Public Prosecutor would submit that these matters are squarely covered by earlier decisions of this court, whereunder the accused against whom similar cases were registered on the basis of similar set of facts were [LEAKAGE_MASK] by this Court as the prosecution is not maintainable against them under law and also on the ground that Tobacco products would not fall within the definition of 'food' as defined under Section 3(i)(j) of FSS Act and that the police are not authorized to register the crime and investigate the same and to file the charge sheet.",
